Curiarium
=========

Curiarium is a fork of MakersVault (https://github.com/GhostLabs-ent/MakersVault),
originally by VincentCinque, MIT licensed. The upstream copyright notice is
retained verbatim in LICENSE; this notice records the relationship so the
attribution travels with the code.

Substantially reworked in this fork, including: filesystem-authoritative folders
and root scanning, trash-backed destructive operations, filesystem snapshot
support (CephFS/ZFS/BTRFS), a per-route permission matrix with boot guards, an
append-only audit log enforced by database triggers, users/roles/OIDC/MFA/session
management, signed file grants replacing bearer tokens in URLs, streamed uploads,
and the project/membership layer.

Upstream work is ported by hand, one ticket at a time, and is not merged or
rebased: the two trees diverged deliberately (see docs/TICKET_WORKFLOW.md and the
fork-stance ticket in the local ticket store).

No trademark rights are claimed over "MakersVault"; "Curiarium" is this fork's
own name.
